  "solution": {
    "text": "Energy of electron in $\\mathrm{n}^{\\text {th }}$ orbit\n$E_n=\\frac{-13.6 e V}{n^2}$\nExcitation energy of electron from $n=1$ to $n=2$\n$E=-13.6\\left[\\frac{1}{2^2}-\\frac{1}{1}\\right]=-13.6\\left[\\frac{1}{4}-\\frac{1}{1}\\right]=10.2 \\mathrm{eV}$",
